    {
      "id": "8f4512ce-13be-4600-b072-144794c466b1",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1072,
        "content": "## Web fetch with Apify\n\nThis workflow fetches content from the web. It first tries n8n's native HTTP Request node, as it is the cheapest option available. If that fails, the workflow calls [Apify Web Fetch](https://apify.com/apify/web-fetch) to retrieve the content. This lets you reach sites with strong anti-bot protection, such as Reddit.\n\n### Setup Steps:\nAll setup is in the *Set Input Parameters* node\n- [ ] Provide list of URLs to fetch\n- [ ]  Provide Apify API token. You can generate one in the [Apify Console](https://console.apify.com/settings/integrations).\n\n### Customizations:\nThis workflow is meant to plug into a larger workflow.\n\nYou can customize how URLs are provided to the workflow. Currently, you need to provide an array in *Set Input Parameters*. \n\nYou can use other options, such as:\n- Get URL from webhook\n- Get URL list from Google Sheets\n\n### Who it's for:\nAnybody trying to get content from a website. Use cases include:\n- Deep research\n- Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)\n- Lead scoring based on web data\n- Market research and competitor analysis"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c5800173-a25d-468a-b13d-3418fdc0985d",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 336,
        "content": "## Manual trigger and input setup\n\nManual start node and nearby setup node that define the URL list and Apify token used by the rest of the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
